>> I'm kind of suprised nobody suggested the obvious: 'use #adjust'.
>> If you adjust the inventory lettering of anything stackable, then it
>> will merge with anything else in your inventory that can stack with
>> it. 
> 
> I'm guessing though, that since he had to pick up the arrow in the
> first place, that all those won't be stackable, or they would have
> stacked in the first place. The ones that are stackable are already
> stacked.
> 
Yes, I think you are correct. I just tried in wizard mode, and after using 
up two arrow traps I had:

f - 3 +0 arrows
g - a +1 arrow
h - a blessed +0 arrow
i - a cursed -3 arrow

So there's a good range of different arrows available, but it is a pretty 
inefficient way of gathering arrows compared with untrapping the trap 
(which gave me 10 blessed +0 arrows).


